M4.25 CI systemd runtime-path diagnosis
Date: 2026-08-28
Failed run: 33198254357
Failed job: restore-contract / Validate M4.25 systemd unit

Observed error
--------------
systemd-analyze rejected the unit because the GitHub runner does not contain
the server-only executable at:

/opt/tu1nz_repos/releases/adult-publishing/staging-s0-commercial/venv-current/bin/tu1nz-commercial-runtime-candidate

Cause
-----
The new CI step executed systemd-analyze directly against the production-path
unit in an ephemeral runner. systemd-analyze validates absolute executable
existence as well as unit syntax. The missing runner path is expected and is
not a unit syntax defect or server drift.

Safety state
------------
No M4.25 server mutation had begun. The candidate remained never started and
the existing unit, manifest, Control link, S1 and backup services were not
changed. No rollback was required.

Versioned correction
--------------------
CI validates a temporary copy in which only the ExecStart executable is
replaced by /bin/true. All other unit directives are byte-preserved for
systemd parsing. Dedicated tests continue to verify the exact versioned
ExecStart, Restart=no, RuntimeMaxSec=180, static structure and network guards.

The M4.25 server controller still runs systemd-analyze against the original
unmodified versioned unit after the immutable release and real runtime path
exist, before any installed-unit replacement. A server-side validation failure
therefore remains fail-closed.

Rollback plan
-------------
If the corrected CI does not pass, stop again with no server change and retain
this diagnosis. Do not bypass the check or install the unit.
